{"step_index":478,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:04:08Z","input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_tokens":238172,"output_tokens":1773,"thinking":"Examining the `renderArea1Code` function within `app.js` to understand how code rendering occurs. The function iterates through raw lines of code data. Initial focus is on understanding the logic flow of rendering each line with consideration to the `step` and `currentSubstep` information.\n\n\nRendering each code line involves highlighting the current step and indicating whether conditional branches are executed or skipped. I'm checking if the current line corresponds to a conditional step to apply the correct badge. The event listener on each row allows stepping to a specific line in the trace.\n\n\n\nAnalyzing the code scroll behavior ensures the active code line remains centered within the container if the content exceeds its visible area. The `renderArea2Teaching` function appears responsible for assembling the visual representation of teaching steps, including code snippets and visual aids.\n\n\nThe code conditionally displays a calculation box based on data availability, revealing a \"before,\" \"calculation,\" and \"after\" sequence. It then presents the meaning of the current step, enhancing it with symbols if relevant. Finally, it addresses the \"why\" of the operation by showing supporting text if it exists.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\app.js","EndLine":825,"StartLine":800,"toolAction":"Viewing lines 800-825 in app.js","toolSummary":"View lines 800-825 in app.js"}}]}
